<BaseLayout title="What I actually look for in a portfolio project | Joey Alvarado">
  <article class="article">
    <p class="eyebrow">Projects</p>
    <h1>What I actually look for in a portfolio project</h1>
    <div class="article-copy">
      <p>I used to think a portfolio project had to be large to count. Now I care more about whether it solves a real problem and whether I understand the decisions inside it.</p>
      <h2>My current bar</h2>
      <p>I want a project to have a clear purpose, instructions that work, and some way to verify the important behavior. A few focused tests are more useful than a long feature list I cannot defend.</p>
      <h2>The part that matters in an interview</h2>
      <p>I should be able to explain what I left out, what broke while I built it, and what I would change next. That is the part that shows whether the project taught me anything.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
